UPDATE public.outreach_email_templates
SET body = E'Dear {{contact_person}},\n\nI am writing from the Global Artist Registry Foundation (GARF), a non-profit Dutch stichting that builds and maintains permanent archives for artists — documentation of their works held under a 100-Year Preservation Plan.\n\nWe would like to invite {{name}} to join as a Supporting Gallery.\n\n**What we are asking — and what we are not asking**\n\nWe ask that you share the documentation you have with all your artists so that each artist can create their own database and archive. We also appreciate it if you encourage your artists to create their own archives and preferably store them at GARF. With the help of our automatic upload, the artist will get their own archive of their works safely stored for at least 100 years.\n\nTo make the handover simple, GARF accepts Excel or CSV files. A ready-made gallery handover template is available in the artist''s GARF account, and the artist can share it with you. We can also parse standard exports from common gallery systems.\n\nTo be completely clear, because it is easy to misread:\n\n- Your records stay exactly where they are. Your database, your inventory system and your files remain untouched and fully under your control.\n- We ask only for a copy — a supplementary archival copy of the documentation relating to the artist''s work — to be placed in the artist''s own GARF archive.\n- Ownership does not move. The documentation in a GARF archive is owned by the artist, not by GARF and not by us. The artist can export or download it at any time.\n- GARF is not a marketplace, a dealer, an agent or a sales platform. It takes no commission and does not broker works. It is an archive.\n\nThe attached document sets out the background, the archival standards we follow, and how the upload works in practice.\n\nIf this is of interest, I would be glad to arrange a short call, or simply send access codes for the artists you represent so they can open their own archives.\n\nWith kind regards,\n\n{{signature}}',
    updated_at = now()
WHERE id = '812ad237-e4d3-4822-be89-8f6a242a597a';

UPDATE public.outreach_email_templates
SET body = E'{{greeting}}\n\nWe are writing on behalf of the Global Artist Registry Foundation (GARF), a Dutch non-profit foundation (stichting) building a permanent, 100-year archival registry for artists and their work. GARF is independent and non-commercial, and it is built to museum and archival standards.\n\n**What we are asking — and what we are not asking**\n\nWe ask that you share the documentation you have with all your artists so that each artist can create their own database and archive. We also appreciate it if you encourage your artists to create their own archives and preferably store them at GARF. With the help of our automatic upload, the artist will get their own archive of their works safely stored for at least 100 years.\n\nTo make the handover simple, GARF accepts Excel or CSV files. A ready-made gallery handover template is available in the artist''s GARF account, and the artist can share it with you. We can also parse standard exports from common gallery systems.\n\nThere are some points we want to be completely clear about, because it is easy to misread. We are not proposing to take over any function your gallery performs, and we are not asking you to hand anything over.\n\n- Your records stay exactly where they are. Your database, your inventory system and your files remain untouched and fully under your control.\n- We ask only for a copy — a supplementary archival copy of the documentation relating to the artist''s work — to be placed in the artist''s own GARF archive.\n- Ownership does not move. The documentation and information in a GARF archive is owned by the artist, not by GARF and not by us. GARF provides the archive; the artist owns the content and can export or download it at any time.\n- GARF is not a marketplace, a dealer, an agent or a sales platform. It takes no commission and does not broker works. It is an an archive.\n\nIf this is of interest, we would welcome a short introductory call or a written reply, and we can walk you through the automated upload for the artists you represent.\n\nWith kind regards,\n\n{{signature}}',
    updated_at = now()
WHERE id = '346db8a8-760a-4e96-9eb0-5c5b42bc0077';